<p>You have not provided an original source. The postcard is a physical copy of an image, the postcard seller does not have original image rights to the image <strong>on</strong> the postcard. They can sell their own physical copy, but don't have intellectual property rights on the image itself. The image is almost certainly public domain, but without an original image source we cannot be sure that this isn't a reproduction under more recent and stringent copyright terms.</p>
<p>Until you can find and provide us with a source proving the image is compatible with the site's image policy you may not readd it to the article and I will be removing it again now. Assuming you find such a source, please contact either myself or LilyFlower before to add the image back to your article.</p>
<p>In the mean time here are 5 different images to choose from on wikimedia commons. I would suggest you save yourself some time and trouble and just use one of these: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Char_2C">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Char_2C</a></p>

